<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.com.omarlahmimi.glutt</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	<array>
		<string>Default</string>
	</array>
	<!-- LOCAL DEVELOPMENT BUILD: the glasses are on Bluetooth Classic.

	     HotspotConfiguration is deliberately ABSENT. It is what lets the toolkit
	     stand up the glasses' softAP, and the softAP is what we are trying not
	     to use: the ExternalAccessory keys in Info.plist select Bluetooth, and
	     removing this entitlement is the belt to that pair of braces. Leave both
	     in place and the toolkit takes the phone off its own Wi-Fi.

	     Measured on real glasses (2026-08-09, aeadecb): first frame in 1.8s on
	     Bluetooth against fifteen to twenty on the softAP, and the phone keeps
	     its own network instead of dropping to cellular for the whole look.

	     `wifi-info` is deliberately KEPT. It is read-only, cannot cause a join,
	     and is the only way NetworkProbe can report which network the phone is
	     actually on, which is the one thing about this feature nobody can see
	     from the outside.

	     BEFORE ANYTHING SHIPS, read docs/glasses-bluetooth.md. Bluetooth needs
	     Meta to authorise `com.meta.ar.wearable` for this bundle id and they
	     declined on issue #266, so a submission has to go back to Wi-Fi:
	     restore HotspotConfiguration here, and the local-network and Bonjour
	     keys in project.yml, and drop the MFi protocol string. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.networking.wifi-info</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
